.TH GAD 1 "" "Gad 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gad \- Queued file transfer manager for KDE
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gad
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Gad manages copies and moves with queuing, pause, resume, verification and restoration. Without arguments, it shows the main window. Commands are forwarded to the existing instance when available.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
Display command help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-background
Start Gad in the system tray without showing its main window.
.TP
.B \-\-copy SOURCE... \-\-to FOLDER
Queue copies of the sources into the destination folder.
.TP
.B \-\-move SOURCE... \-\-to FOLDER
Queue moves of the sources into the destination folder.
.TP
.B \-\-paste FOLDER
Queue clipboard files into the destination. Cut clipboard data requests a move. Starts the transfer without opening the main window.
.TP
.B \-\-paste\-current
Paste into the active supported Dolphin or Konqueror folder. Requires the corresponding file manager integration.
.TP
.B \-\-paste\-context URL...
Paste using the folder or selected file context supplied by a KIO service menu.
.TP
.B \-\-md5
Verify source and destination contents using MD5 for the submitted transfer. Does not change the saved preference.
.TP
.B \-\-properties
Verify visible owners, groups, permissions, ACLs and extended attributes for the submitted transfer. This checks properties; it does not replicate them. Does not change the saved preference.
.TP
.B \-\-status
Print the current engine state as JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-smoke\-test
Run an isolated graphical startup check with temporary storage.
.TP
.B gad://show
Show the main window of the running instance.
.TP
.B \-\-configure OPTIONS...
Save settings in the running instance, or start Gad in the tray to save them. Requires at least one setting. Boolean switches listed below must be used with \-\-configure; use their \-\-no\- form to disable them.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-md5, \-\-no\-properties
With \-\-configure, disable the corresponding verification preference. \-\-configure \-\-md5 and \-\-configure \-\-properties enable it.
.TP
.B \-\-verify\-space, \-\-no\-verify\-space
With \-\-configure, enable or disable available space checks for new transfers.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-history, \-\-no\-keep\-history
With \-\-configure, enable or disable persistent transfer history.
.TP
.B \-\-resume\-interrupted, \-\-no\-resume\-interrupted
With \-\-configure, enable or disable durable checkpoints and automatic recovery for new transfers.
.TP
.B \-\-include\-hidden, \-\-no\-include\-hidden
With \-\-configure, include or exclude hidden items. Keep existing exclusion patterns.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-duplication, \-\-no\-allow\-duplication
With \-\-configure, enable or disable copies named name_copied1 in the source folder.
.TP
.B \-\-autostart, \-\-no\-autostart
With \-\-configure, enable or disable launching Gad when the current user signs in.
.TP
.B \-\-konqueror\-ctrl\-v, \-\-no\-konqueror\-ctrl\-v
With \-\-configure, enable or disable paste interception in Konqueror launched with Gad. The integration plugin must be installed.
.TP
.B \-\-language LOCALE
With \-\-configure, select system or an installed locale such as fr_FR or en_US.
.TP
.B \-\-rate\-limit MIB_PER_SECOND
With \-\-configure, set the global speed limit in MiB/s; 0 means unlimited. Applies immediately.
.TP
.B \-\-exclude\-folder PATTERN, \-\-exclude\-file PATTERN
With \-\-configure, replace the corresponding pattern list. Repeat an option for multiple patterns; quote shell wildcards. Unspecified lists remain unchanged.
.TP
.B \-\-clear\-exclusions
With \-\-configure, clear both pattern lists. Later pattern options add rules. Does not change hidden item handling.
.TP
.B \-\-dolphin\-ctrl\-v, \-\-no\-dolphin\-ctrl\-v
With \-\-configure, enable or disable Ctrl+V integration in Dolphin. Restart Dolphin after changing it.
.SH PATHS
Sources and destinations accept local paths and file, ftp, sftp, smb and kdeconnect URLs supported by KIO Fuse. The relevant services and mounts must be available. Quote paths containing spaces.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
gad \-\-copy "/home/user/My file.txt" \-\-to /media/backup \-\-md5
gad \-\-move /home/user/file.txt \-\-to /media/archive \-\-properties
gad \-\-paste /media/backup
gad \-\-status
gad \-\-configure \-\-dolphin\-ctrl\-v \-\-konqueror\-ctrl\-v
gad \-\-configure \-\-rate\-limit 25 \-\-exclude\-folder "__*" \-\-exclude\-file "*.tmp"
.fi
.SH SETTINGS
Options supplied with \-\-configure are persistent and reflected in graphical settings. New transfers use saved preferences unless explicitly overridden. Not all settings apply retroactively to existing transfers. Configure Ctrl+V in Dolphin with \-\-configure \-\-dolphin\-ctrl\-v or \-\-no\-dolphin\-ctrl\-v.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/gad/docs/
HTML and PDF guides in the supported languages.
